Subject: [PATCH] TVP Timer: validate interval before integer conversion

Reject negative, non-finite and over-one-day timer intervals before the
floating-point to signed-integer cast. This is the audited bounded Android
scheduler contract; it prevents undefined conversion in the upstream setter.

Tested-by: tests/test_krkr_tjs2_source_admission.py focused git-apply unittest; forced Android CMake configure; Krkr Timer instrumentation

--- a/src/core/utils/TimerIntf.cpp
+++ b/src/core/utils/TimerIntf.cpp
@@ -201,6 +201,8 @@
 	{
 		TJS_GET_NATIVE_INSTANCE(/*var. name*/_this, /*var. type*/tTJSNI_Timer);
 		double interval = (double)*param * (1<<TVP_SUBMILLI_FRAC_BITS);
+		if(!(interval >= 0 && interval <= 86400000.0 * (1<<TVP_SUBMILLI_FRAC_BITS)))
+			return TJS_E_INVALIDPARAM;
 		_this->SetInterval((tjs_int64)(interval + 0.5));
 		return TJS_S_OK;
 	}
